# Documentation Standards

## Knowledge Graph Structure
- All documentation folders must have an index.md file
- All documents must link to related documents through relative links
- Each document should include a "Related Documentation" section
- Cross-references should be bidirectional
- Documentation should be structured with clear entry points

## Documentation Content
- Document both the "why" and "how" for significant decisions
- Include examples for core functionality
- Use Markdown tables for complex data
- Include diagrams for complex relationships
- Keep documents concise and focused
- Use consistent terminology throughout

## Maintenance
- Update documentation immediately when code or decisions change
- Remove outdated or redundant information immediately
- Store project management documents in docs/project-management
- Update implementation plan when completing tasks

## Documentation Types
- Architecture documentation should explain system components and relationships
- Decision records should include context, options, decision, and consequences
- Specifications should provide detailed technical requirements
- Guides should provide step-by-step instructions
- Project management documents should track progress against clearly defined criteria
